- ROADMAP.md:310: A decreasing nonnegative variant bounds iterations or recursive edges along a path, not total execution steps. For example, a function making two calls with measure `n - 1` has exponential total work despite entry measure `n`; a loop body may also contain an explicitly permitted nonterminating call. Automatic step bounds require separate body/callee bounds and composition of all calls before they can support the facts ledger’s cost claims.
