- ROADMAP.md:585: Body-only edits cannot unconditionally permit downstream codegen reuse. Changing a generic function’s implementation can leave its signature, contracts and exported facts unchanged while requiring callers’ specializations to be regenerated; inlined callers have the same problem. Restrict reuse to artifacts that depend only on the interface, and invalidate body-dependent artifacts using `body_hash`, or incremental builds can execute stale code.
- ROADMAP.md:596: The bitmask rule omits the unsigned/non-negative-mask condition present in the linked proposal. Under `Scalar.bitwise`, signed `i8` values `x = -1` and `mask = -1` produce `-1`, contradicting `0 ≤ (x & mask) ≤ mask`. Restore that condition so the roadmap does not require a false transfer theorem.
